{%- comment -%}
  Converts an AUD cent amount into the buyer's presentment currency.

  Shipping rates and free-shipping minimums are configured in AUD in the
  Shopify admin, but the storefront renders in the buyer's currency. Passing an
  AUD figure straight to the `money` filter would print "€250" for what is
  really A$250 — a number the buyer never has to reach. This converts first.

  Outputs a bare integer (cents) so callers can coerce and format:
    {%- capture c -%}{%- render 'aud-to-presentment', cents: 25000 -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign c = c | plus: 0 -%}
    {{ c | money }}

  Rates live in settings.fx_rates_from_aud (Theme settings → Currency) so they
  can be refreshed without a code change. A currency that isn't listed falls
  back to 1:1, which shows the AUD figure rather than an invented one.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign target = cart.currency.iso_code | default: shop.currency
  assign out = cents

  if target != 'AUD'
    assign pairs = settings.fx_rates_from_aud | default: '' | split: ','
    for pair in pairs
      assign kv = pair | strip | split: ':'
      assign code = kv[0] | strip
      assign rate = kv[1] | strip | plus: 0.0
      if code == target and rate > 0
        assign out = cents | times: rate | round
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
{{- out -}}
